VeridianOS: kmimetypefinder: report errors reading standard input

GCC reported -Wunused-result for QFile::open(FILE *, ...) in main()
(kmimetypefinder/kmimetypefinder.cpp), used for the "-" (read from stdin)
argument.

Small real bug, though not where the warning points (a read-only open of
stdin does not fail in Qt 6): the read was not checked. With stdin a
directory or closed, readAll() returned an empty buffer,
QMimeDatabase::mimeTypeForData() classified it as application/x-zerosize,
and the tool printed that and exited 0, as if stdin had been an empty
file. The open and the read are now checked; an error is printed on
stdout, the way the tool reports its other errors, with exit status 1.
The normal path is unchanged. (Prepared for upstream,
invent.kde.org/plasma/kde-cli-tools.)

--- a/kmimetypefinder/kmimetypefinder.cpp
+++ b/kmimetypefinder/kmimetypefinder.cpp
@@ -47,8 +47,15 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     QMimeType mime;
     if (fileName == QLatin1String("-")) {
         QFile qstdin;
-        qstdin.open(stdin, QIODevice::ReadOnly);
+        if (!qstdin.open(stdin, QIODevice::ReadOnly)) {
+            printf("Could not open standard input: %s\n", qPrintable(qstdin.errorString()));
+            return 1;
+        }
         const QByteArray data = qstdin.readAll();
+        if (qstdin.error() != QFile::NoError) {
+            printf("Could not read standard input: %s\n", qPrintable(qstdin.errorString()));
+            return 1;
+        }
         mime = db.mimeTypeForData(data);
     } else if (parser.isSet(QStringLiteral("c"))) {
         mime = db.mimeTypeForFile(fileName, QMimeDatabase::MatchContent);
